      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Warichu (inline double-column note) under the 外高, read right sub-column (込高井前) then left (々新田共): the 199.92195 koku consists of komidaka — koku already folded into the combined total — together with previously-opened new paddy (shinden). Here 井 stands for 并 'and also', the same usage attested in the HI at Hitoyoshi (込高井新田高); 前々 'former' is attested at Saijō (前々拜領高)."
      },
